harness:platform/resourceGroup:ResourceG.description:
A **Resource Group** defines the **set of Harness resources** that fall within an RBAC boundary (for example, all pipelines, selected connectors, or specific secrets), along with the **scopes** (account, organization, or project) where the group applies.

When configuring a resource group, you typically control access using two dimensions:

* **Scopes** – where the resource group applies (<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`includedScopes`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`IncludedScopes`" pulumi-lang-go="`includedScopes`" pulumi-lang-python="`included_scopes`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`includedScopes`" pulumi-lang-java="`includedScopes`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`included_scopes`">`includedScopes`</span>)
* **Resources** – what resources are included (<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`resourceFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ResourceFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`resourceFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`resource_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`resourceFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`resourceFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`resource_filter`">`resourceFilter`</span>)

